WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.620
I live in New York state,

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.000
one of many where

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.880
politicians spend more money than we have.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.240
There’s a $4.4 billion dollar deficit.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.190
My governor wants to raise taxes,

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.600
but this man says

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.480
there's a better way to raise money.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.900
We can lease naming rights on our infrastructure.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:16.580
We can use…

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:17.660
Infrastructure meaning…

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.600
Bridges, tunnels,

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.840
The Triborough bridge could be called

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.087
the Staples Bridge,

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:23.400
or the Apple Bridge.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.523
Companies would pay

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:27.300
because bridges are seen by lots of people.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.340
Hundreds of thousands of vehicles pass by,

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.700
and see that big sign.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.700
That’s valuable.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.140
That I disagree with.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.480
That's a bad idea.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.260
Most people we asked didn’t like the idea.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.260
I definitely wouldn't want to rename something

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.600
after some sort of corporation.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.060
People don’t like this.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.640
It’s commercializing!

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:45.649
Absolutely.

00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:46.460
Shake your fist and say

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.400
“this doesn’t sound good”

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.539
if you want to.

00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:50.260
And you’re going to wind up in a place where

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.510
the tax burden is insanely high.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.380
I just think some things should be left pure,

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.000
not tainted by money.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:56.969
You know what she should do?

00:00:56.969 --> 00:00:58.400
Start a nonprofit,

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.637
raise 30 million dollars,

00:00:59.637 --> 00:01:01.369
she can name it whatever she wants.

00:01:01.369 --> 00:01:03.860
It’s one of the largest construction projects

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.000
in the country.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.260
Our governor just had a beautiful new bridge built

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.509
and he named it after his father.

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:10.240
Yes he did.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:10.980
That’s true.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.820
Governor Mario M. Cuomo bridge.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.449
We actually have an imperial bridge

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:15.799
named after our royal family.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:16.840
I’m embarrassed.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.620
Sharpe is the libertarian candidate.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.120
We libertarians don’t worship politicians

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.429
and don’t think they deserve monuments,

00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:25.840
just because they got elected.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:26.899
I’ll tell you what I’ll do.

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:28.179
He’s got 30 million dollars a year?

00:01:28.179 --> 00:01:29.560
He can keep his name on that bridge

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.720
and he needs to take care of the maintenance.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.860
Someone asked me,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.020
Larry, how are you going to pay for I-81?

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.780
Sharpe’s campaign is attracting new people.

00:01:36.789 --> 00:01:38.760
His rallies have bigger crowds

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.640
than third party candidates normally get.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.564
And Sharpe’s original ideas

00:01:43.564 --> 00:01:45.080
helped get him speaking roles

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.242
at big events

00:01:46.242 --> 00:01:47.940
and media coverage.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.260
If you’re unhappy with the system,

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.160
you’ve got to change it.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.400
One poll found Sharpe getting 13%

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.780
and after people hear his campaign pitch,

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:59.060
25% support him.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.180
I’m not gonna roll back anything.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.840
Some of Sharpe's positions surprised me.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.880
You're a libertarian.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.740
I assume you want to cut these wasteful programs.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.500
Of course not.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.480
Look, the issue here is

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.620
you don't want to just pull the rug out from people

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.560
because when you do that, they become afraid.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.040
If people are afraid,

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.240
they rarely vote for you.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.920
So you would keep all these government programs?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.239
When did I say that was going away?

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:20.840
Yeah.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.900
I said no new programs.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.440
And you would keep the existing-

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.440
Sure.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.260
Why ... who said I would get rid of them?

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:26.760
I never said that.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:27.920
I just assumed because

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:28.540
Why?

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.040
They're inefficient, they're bloated, they're-

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:30.760
So get rid of them?

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.900
That's the worst idea.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.400
Let me be very clear about something.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.680
If you pull the rug out from somebody,

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.650
somebody's going to be afraid.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.010
Sharpe focuses on his alternatives to taxes.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.920
Why don’t we instead have a 3M bridge

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.280
or a Apple bridge,

00:02:44.283 --> 00:02:45.560
or a Pepsi bridge?

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.880
Why hasn’t this been done?

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.320
Because no one has any new ideas.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.200
There’s no ideas how I’m going to fix anything

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.060
or do anything right.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.060
It doesn’t even exist.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:52.880
I’m a third party.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.320
I have to have ideas

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.620
or no one will listen to me.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.420
The MTA, New York's subway system,

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.020
is falling apart.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.060
Trains are packed, buses are packed.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.200
We need the money.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.300
So Sharpe says,

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.660
rent out the tracks at night.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.580
We have so many lines on the MTA right now

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.620
that are not being used at all at night.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.260
Home Depot or Google or Amazon

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.080
or whomever,

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:15.900
they can decide

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.040
they can use these freight lines,

00:03:17.049 --> 00:03:18.755
they’ll help pay for maintenance obviously

00:03:18.755 --> 00:03:20.299
and they’ll pay to move their freight.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.800
Again, win-win-win.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.519
Then Sharpe said something else that surprised me.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.840
There are systems out there

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.000
that are both safe and unionized,

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.020
so we keep the unions happy

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.047
and our workers safe,

00:03:30.047 --> 00:03:30.780
and be cheaper.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.180
Why do you want to keep the unions happy?

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.480
Because they're unionized?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.340
Why would I want not to keep unions happy?

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:38.580
Because unions can be destructive.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:39.540
They can be, absolutely.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.160
I don’t think of a libertarian as a pro-union guy.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.340
Unions are part of our First Amendment.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:45.420
It's people getting together

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.140
saying they won't do X until you do Y.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.180
Nothing wrong with that at all.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.740
It raises prices.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:51.940
Fine, that's okay.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:52.660
It is what it is.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.420
Collective bargaining is fine.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.320
My issue with the unions has always been

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.020
are you forcing me to be in a union?

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.880
Are you forcing unionized labor?

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.030
If you're forcing it, I'm libertarian.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.360
I have a problem with that,

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.300
but you're voluntarily doing it?

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.450
I don't have a problem at all.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:07.183
Sharpe is the rare politician

00:04:07.183 --> 00:04:08.520
who proposes new ideas

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.769
that might actually reduce the burden

00:04:10.769 --> 00:04:12.220
of government.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:14.680
This man liked his subway-funding idea.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:15.700
I think that would be good.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.140
We need air conditioning in the subways,

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.090
so Amazon, get us air conditioning.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.360
He’s thinking the right way.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.720
Amazon will love it, we’ll love it.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:23.880
I like that guy.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.620
And I like it that there’s at least one candidate

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.500
who doesn’t want to make government

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.500
bigger.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.440
New programs?

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.080
No. I'm libertarian.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:32.960
No new programs?

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.640
No no no no no no no no.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.080
That are going to take care of people?

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.140
You do know what party I am part of, right?

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:39.240
Libertarians believe

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.060
that you should be as conservative

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.940
or as liberal as you want to be,

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:46.660
as long as you don’t want to force yourself on others.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:50.240
Larry Sharpe for Governor 2018.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.500
Thank you very much.

